{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'rg -n \"prize|ERC-721|malicious|trust|code.length|NotContract|factory|sponsor\" DESIGN.md WORKSPACE.md packages/contracts/src/interfaces/*.sol'","aggregated_output":"DESIGN.md:2:Ethereum NFT raffle; immutable factory, ERC-1167 clones with immutable implementation. One entry costs 1,000,000 units of canonical six-decimal USDC. One purchase mints a transferable ERC721 ticket representing a contiguous inclusive range. Exactly one ERC721 prize is escrowed atomically at creation. Reserve met awards NFT and 95% sponsor / 5% treasury. Reserve missed awards 80% gross to winner, 15% sponsor, 5% treasury. Refund outcome pays 100% per entry and returns prize. Rounding is floor on aggregate protocol fee; remainder must be allocated without loss. No administrator, mutable configuration or upgrade. Request window [sale end, end+2days); callback accepted strictly before request timestamp+2days. Refunds open at deadline. Callback records result only. Settlement is permissionless, storage-only; redemption requires current ticket owner, burns claim atomically, and must revert all effects on delivery failure. Sponsor and treasury can claim independently after settlement. Never move assets between raffle clones. Quote token and Chainlink wrapper are trusted canonical dependencies; arbitrary prize contracts and ticket recipients are untrusted. Frontend discovery is advisory; transaction decisions must reread current chain state.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:10:/// @notice Defines one autonomous NFT raffle using fixed-price USDC entries and one transferable ERC-721 ticket per\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:13:///      bearer claim until its owner atomically burns it for redemption or refund. The immutable quote token is trusted\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:14:///      canonical six-decimal USDC with standard, non-rebasing, fee-free transfers. Supported prizes are honest,\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:15:///      standards-compliant ERC-721s.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:22:        /// @notice The clone is initialized and waiting for the factory to escrow the configured prize.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:24:        /// @notice The prize is escrowed and entry sales or post-sale draw initiation are available.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:28:        /// @notice The reserve was met and the winning ticket may redeem the prize NFT.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:32:        /// @notice Full ticket refunds are enabled and the sponsor may recover the prize NFT.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:36:    /// @notice Complete clone-specific configuration supplied once by the canonical factory.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:37:    /// @param sponsor Prize depositor and empty-raffle cancellation authority.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:38:    /// @param sponsorRecipient Immutable recipient of sponsor quote proceeds and any returned prize.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:40:    /// @param prizeToken Standards-compliant ERC-721 prize contract.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:41:    /// @param prizeTokenId Token ID of the prize escrowed by this raffle.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:42:    /// @param raffleId One-based canonical factory identifier for this raffle.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:46:        address sponsor;\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:47:        address sponsorRecipient;\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:49:        address prizeToken;\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:50:        uint256 prizeTokenId;\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:58:    /// @notice Emitted when the factory deposits the configured prize and activates the raffle.\npackages/contracts/s